  "spice_vs_liberty_caveat": "The decks drive a 5 ps (0-100%) input edge while the liberty figures are interpolated at a 10 ps (10-90%) slew; from the short-circuit sweep that is worth under 0.01 fJ per cycle for INVx1, so it does not change the sign of any row. The liberty is characterised at 0.7 V, so only the 0.7 V decks are compared with it.",
  "spice_vs_liberty_verdict": "At 0.7 V and 2 fF, with the arc, the state and the set of outputs driven all matched, the schematic netlist runs 0.90x (INVx1 A [(any)]) to 1.36x (XOR2x1 A [B]) of the liberty's VDD-only figure, over 8 cases. IT GOES BOTH WAYS. So a schematic SPICE energy is NOT a general lower bound on the extracted one: the first version of this file said it was, generalising from the inverter alone, and carried the 2.04x schematic-vs-extracted DELAY ratio across to energy with no measurement behind it. Corrected in review the same day. The only honest statement is that the two agree to within about +-35% per case, with no systematic sign.",
